# plugins/ and opencode/ are committed build output: a CRLF checkout on Windows would make every
# rebuild look like a diff, so normalise line endings in the working tree, not just the index.
* text=auto eol=lf
# A unified diff represents an empty context line as one space. Do not treat that required nested
# patch syntax as trailing whitespace when the outer repository diff reviews a recut overlay.
overlays/**/overlay.patch whitespace=-blank-at-eol
# The dispatch tests' fixtures (canned backend streams, a pinned Codex schema) are compared byte for
# byte, so Git stores and checks them out exactly as committed, with no line-ending conversion.
tests/dispatch/fixtures/** -text
# external/ submodules contain symlinks; checking them out on Windows needs core.symlinks=true
# (enabled by Developer Mode or an elevated clone), otherwise git writes them as plain text files.
